ell me that you know what am i good at  oh i'm a perfectionist okay great you  know that's just a glib answer to the  question  so for me the crucible decisions  one of them was to join mckinsey  when i qualified as an actuary i took a  50 pay cut relative to what i would have  been earning as an actuary to join  mckinsey  and i had to pay back the bursary that  i'd gotten from the insurance company so  it was a double whammy financially and  the bursary is effectively a scholarship  college yeah but you have to pay back if  you don't go work for them so the the  deal was that they would pay for my  tuition and i had to work for them for  the same number of years that i studied  to pay off the debt and if i didn't work  for them i literally had to pay them  back every penny and so  so i earned less and had the debt to pay  off i made the same decision when i  joined paypal  so i had  mckinsey was paying for some of my  tuition at stanford and i had to pay  them back  and what i was getting i still have my  offer letter elon recruited me to to  paypal  x.com and i have the signed offer letter  still on my door and uh i got 80 000  that was my salary when i finished  my mba in 2000 and it was less than  mckinsey was going to pay me  and i had to pay mckinsey back  and then the third one was joining  sequoia and those are the three key  career decisions  you

